<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia coffee growers federation sets '97 budget.</title>
<headline>Colombia coffee growers federation sets '97 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's National Federation of Coffee Growers announced Tuesday its 1997 budget would be 146.7 billion pesos, a nominal 5.5 percent increase compared to this year.</p>
<p>Of that total, 56.5 percent will be directed to infrastructure projects, 10.7 percent to scientific research and 12.4 percent to operational activities including domestic and export sales promotion, a statement from the federation said.</p>
<p>With inflation to November running at almost 21 percent, the 1997 budget represents a cut in real terms.</p>
<p>&quot;The 1997 budget reflects the austerity policy and a cut in expenditure and investment,&quot; a statement from the federation said.</p>
<p>-- Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
</text>
